{"title":"Factoring Quadratics","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The purpose of factoring a quadratic is to turn the quadratic into a product of 2 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial\" title=\"Binomial\">binomials</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Method_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Method 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Example\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Limitations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Limitations</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Method_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Method 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Example_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Limitations_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Limitations</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Also_See\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Also See</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Method_1\">Method 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Method 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Method 1 starts with factoring the product of the roots. Let the quadratic we are factoring be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/98172d1b54b563033d26dc22c407dad4d4802be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2+bx+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />. When factored, it will be in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec86197d724becc0abcb624e98f7869d17200e2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a(x-r)(x-s)=0,\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of the quadratic, and where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e84bf3cc7f530d9d46910372ae776fac1f3935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s=-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f0f8a44b450f01df473758b49e5b15e8ad312a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\cdot s=c$\" width=\"62\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example\">Example</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Example\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8b0f847734549eed34588cfb048efd0c733a96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-8x+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Since the coefficient on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we know are quadratic factors in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5c1d8ab857f150325f70d4a8fbe1e845c3b89a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-r)(x-s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />. We know that the factor pairs of 12 are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920d739d4f4ce60f1cd42ca937257d659492bb01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,12), (2,6), (3,4), (4,3), (6,2), (1,12), (-1,-12), (-2,-6), (-3,-4), (-4,-3), (-6,-2),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"697\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c4acbbf8c6af2cec42b47b6b419c3f3143592a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-12,-1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> We can find that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd87710da1743ebb0de8c0d280b13a036d422fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/49872c1a93c707dd850a4c311b1e6eadacc58500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy our equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e84bf3cc7f530d9d46910372ae776fac1f3935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s=-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f0f8a44b450f01df473758b49e5b15e8ad312a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\cdot s=c$\" width=\"62\" height=\"8\" />, so the factored form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8b0f847734549eed34588cfb048efd0c733a96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-8x+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e52453c82e571664135e0a7311f01abfe4f9271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2)(x-6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Limitations\">Limitations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Limitations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>This method cannot be used to factor quadratics with complex or irrational roots.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Method_2\">Method 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Method 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Method 2 starts by using the sum. Let the quadratic we are factoring be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/98172d1b54b563033d26dc22c407dad4d4802be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2+bx+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />. When factored, it will be in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec86197d724becc0abcb624e98f7869d17200e2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a(x-r)(x-s)=0,\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of the quadratic, and where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e84bf3cc7f530d9d46910372ae776fac1f3935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s=-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f0f8a44b450f01df473758b49e5b15e8ad312a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\cdot s=c$\" width=\"62\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_2\">Example</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Example\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c4b9c5ada4a5798ddb504ad09dc6cbc71b8e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-8x+13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9114c281c42eb25d783e5fa62c20f519e19cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s=-(-8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, so we can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f8d353b67d3ba636c9c9e87998ec26a51d5f28e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=4-u$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/454d6de2e5d855df7d82be21f746cf6be75c8575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=4+u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />. Then, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47cc0e98109e97cc15800f782c1e89023149c3c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\cdot s= 16-u^2 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"154\" height=\"15\" />, giving us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7315769f34ae818f8648c004a36dc9dd63f626a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2=3$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0015215261755637f9c107a67fea6097979908b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=\\pm \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. Because we have both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/d/88d753947813ebf13c9b5e69c15de98f65bda764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-u$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d7707ca71f6fb8995e849fc06635bb859086cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> as our roots, it doesn't matter which one is plugged in, giving us that the factored form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c4b9c5ada4a5798ddb504ad09dc6cbc71b8e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-8x+13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cf55367a88a4382b5c66d97787de103af965caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x-\\left(4+\\sqrt{3}\\right)\\right)\\left(x-\\left(4-\\sqrt{3}\\right)\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"261\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Limitations_2\">Limitations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Limitations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>None currently known.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Also_See\">Also See</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Also See\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation\" title=\"Quadratic equation\">Quadratic equation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring\" title=\"Factoring\">Factoring</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017111637\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 197/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6186/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17904:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017111637 and revision id 289429. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}